('115.26.b.4.D',3,'In the decision-making process, the first step is usually to...','["flip a coin", "act without thinking", "ignore options", "identify the problem or choice"]'::jsonb,3,'Start by defining the decision.','original'),
('115.26.b.4.D',3,'After choosing a solution in decision-making, a person should...','["evaluate how it worked", "forget it", "never think about it again", "blame others"]'::jsonb,0,'Reflection improves future decisions.','original'),
('115.26.b.5.A',3,'Adolescent brain development helps explain why teens may...','["lose memory at 12", "feel strong emotions and take more risks", "never feel anything", "stop growing at age 10"]'::jsonb,1,'The brain is still maturing during adolescence.','original'),
('115.26.b.5.A',3,'The part of the brain that helps with planning and judgment continues developing until...','["age 8", "age 10", "the early to mid twenties", "age 6"]'::jsonb,2,'The prefrontal cortex matures late.','original'),
('115.26.b.5.B',3,'A positive school climate can help students by...','["ignoring bullying", "limiting healthy food", "causing more stress", "making them feel safe and supported"]'::jsonb,3,'Climate affects health behaviors.','original'),
('115.26.b.5.B',3,'Having healthy food available at school supports...','["better nutrition choices", "junk food only", "worse concentration", "more absences"]'::jsonb,0,'Available options shape what students choose.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.A',3,'A healthy way to manage change is to...','["avoid everything", "talk with someone supportive and make a plan", "pretend nothing happened", "act out angrily"]'::jsonb,1,'Healthy coping reduces stress.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.A',3,'An unhealthy method of managing a big change is...','["exercise", "journaling", "bottling up feelings until you explode", "asking for help"]'::jsonb,2,'Suppressing feelings can lead to bigger problems.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.B',3,'A lifetime strategy for managing a chronic condition like asthma includes...','["stopping medicine without asking", "hiding it from others", "ignoring symptoms", "following a treatment plan and avoiding triggers"]'::jsonb,3,'Management is ongoing.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.B',3,'A person with a long-term health condition should...','["have regular checkups and follow medical advice", "skip medicines", "avoid all doctors", "ignore symptoms"]'::jsonb,0,'Regular care keeps conditions under control.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.C',3,'Resiliency means...','["avoiding every problem", "bouncing back from difficult events", "never feeling sad", "giving up quickly"]'::jsonb,1,'Resilient people recover and grow.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.C',3,'A way to build resiliency is to...','["avoid challenges", "blame yourself for everything", "keep a supportive network and learn from setbacks", "isolate yourself"]'::jsonb,2,'Support and learning build resilience.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.D',3,'A healthy way to manage stress is...','["skipping meals", "picking fights", "staying up all night", "deep breathing and exercise"]'::jsonb,3,'Healthy coping lowers stress.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.D',3,'An unhealthy way to deal with stress is...','["using substances to escape", "talking to a friend", "listening to music", "taking a walk"]'::jsonb,0,'Substances create bigger problems.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.E',3,'Disordered eating can be harmful because it...','["builds strong bones", "can damage physical and emotional health", "improves energy for everyone", "is a normal diet"]'::jsonb,1,'Eating disorders are serious illnesses.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.E',3,'If a friend seems to have an unhealthy relationship with food, a good step is to...','["tease them", "join them", "encourage them to talk to a trusted adult", "ignore it forever"]'::jsonb,2,'Trusted adults can connect them with help.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.F',3,'A protective factor that helps lower a teen''s suicide risk is...','["avoiding help", "access to harmful items", "isolation from everyone", "strong connections with family, friends and caring adults"]'::jsonb,3,'Support and connection protect.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.F',3,'A warning sign that a friend may need help is...','["talking about feeling hopeless or withdrawing from everyone", "laughing at a movie", "joining a club", "getting good grades"]'::jsonb,0,'Changes in mood and behavior matter.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.G',3,'A healthy self-concept helps avoid self-harm by...','["comparing yourself to everyone", "building a sense of worth and ways to ask for help", "hiding pain", "ignoring feelings"]'::jsonb,1,'Self-worth supports safe coping.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.G',3,'When someone feels overwhelmed, a safe choice is to...','["stay alone", "avoid friends", "tell a trusted adult how they are feeling", "keep it secret"]'::jsonb,2,'Reaching out is a strength.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.H',3,'In the United States, you can call or text this number for the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline:','["311", "211", "411", "988"]'::jsonb,3,'988 connects people with trained counselors.','original'),
('115.26.b.6.H',3,'A school resource that can help a student in emotional distress is...','["a counselor", "a bus schedule", "a vending machine", "a locker"]'::jsonb,0,'Counselors are trained to help.','original'),
('115.26.b.7.A',3,'Calcium helps the body mainly by building...','["longer hair", "strong bones and teeth", "sharper eyesight", "faster running only"]'::jsonb,1,'Calcium is a bone mineral.','original'),
('115.26.b.7.A',3,'Iron is needed to...','["grow taller overnight", "digest sugar", "help blood carry oxygen", "block sunlight"]'::jsonb,2,'Iron is part of hemoglobin.','original'),
('115.26.b.7.B',3,'When comparing two cereals, a student should check the Nutrition Facts for...','["the font size", "the box color", "the brand logo", "added sugars and fiber"]'::jsonb,3,'Labels let you compare nutrition.','original'),
('115.26.b.7.B',3,'Menus that list calories help diners...','["compare nutritional content before ordering", "avoid reading", "order randomly", "guess portion sizes"]'::jsonb,0,'Calorie labeling aids choices.','original'),
('115.26.b.7.C',3,'A healthy dietary practice is...','["drinking soda instead of water", "eating a variety of fruits and vegetables", "skipping breakfast daily", "eating only candy"]'::jsonb,1,'Variety provides nutrients.','original'),
