('115.26.b.13.E',3,'A sign that someone online may be trying to manipulate you is that they...','["talk about hobbies", "encourage you to do homework", "share a joke", "ask you to keep secrets from your parents"]'::jsonb,3,'Secrecy is a red flag.','original'),
('115.26.b.13.F',3,'Cyberbullying can have legal consequences such as...','["police involvement or fines in some cases", "no response", "a free pass", "a trophy"]'::jsonb,0,'Laws address harassment online.','original'),
('115.26.b.13.F',3,'In Texas, sharing inappropriate images of a minor is...','["harmless", "illegal and can lead to serious penalties", "legal if deleted later", "allowed with friends"]'::jsonb,1,'Such content is against the law.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.A',3,'Exposure to family violence can cause a child to...','["gain confidence immediately", "become healthier", "feel scared, anxious or struggle in school", "do better in class"]'::jsonb,2,'Violence affects emotional well-being.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.A',3,'A child who sees violence at home should...','["keep it secret", "copy the behavior", "blame themselves", "talk to a trusted adult such as a counselor"]'::jsonb,3,'Help is available.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.B',3,'A healthy way to respond to bullying is to...','["stay calm, walk away and tell an adult", "ignore and hide", "post about it angrily", "bully back"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe responses reduce harm.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.B',3,'A bystander can discourage bullying by...','["watching silently", "refusing to join in and supporting the victim", "recording it for fun", "laughing"]'::jsonb,1,'Bystander support helps.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.C',3,'Bullying can lead victims to feel...','["popular", "excited about school", "anxious, lonely and afraid to go to school", "more confident"]'::jsonb,2,'Bullying harms mental health.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.C',3,'People who bully others may also face...','["awards", "less trouble", "better friendships", "discipline and social problems"]'::jsonb,3,'Bullying has consequences for the bully too.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.D',3,'A school strategy to prevent bullying is...','["clear rules and anonymous reporting", "no supervision", "punishing victims", "ignoring reports"]'::jsonb,0,'Prevention needs rules and reporting.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.D',3,'Intervening safely in bullying includes...','["fighting the bully", "getting an adult to help", "making a joke of it", "ignoring it"]'::jsonb,1,'Adults can stop it safely.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.E',3,'A trusted adult you can ask for input on a problem could be...','["a rumor", "an anonymous chat", "a parent, teacher or counselor", "a stranger online"]'::jsonb,2,'Trusted adults give guidance.','original'),
('115.26.b.14.E',3,'Seeking input from a trusted adult helps because they can...','["make decisions for you always", "ignore you", "tell everyone", "offer experience and support"]'::jsonb,3,'Advice can guide choices.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.A',3,'Misusing a prescription drug means...','["taking it in a way not prescribed or taking someone else''s", "following the label", "asking the pharmacist a question", "taking the prescribed dose"]'::jsonb,0,'Misuse is dangerous.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.A',3,'Sharing your prescription medicine with a friend is...','["recommended", "dangerous and may be illegal", "kind", "safe"]'::jsonb,1,'Medicine is prescribed for one person.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.B',3,'An over-the-counter medicine is one that...','["needs a doctor''s note", "is only for adults in hospitals", "can be bought without a prescription", "is illegal"]'::jsonb,2,'OTC medicines are sold in stores.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.B',3,'Prescription drugs differ from OTC drugs because they...','["are free", "have no side effects", "are always weaker", "require a doctor''s order"]'::jsonb,3,'Prescriptions require professional oversight.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.C',3,'To safely store medicine at home, keep it...','["in a locked or high place away from children", "in a backpack", "on the counter", "in a bathroom drawer open"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe storage prevents poisoning.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.C',3,'To dispose of unused medicine safely, use...','["leaving it in the trash openly", "a drug take-back program or pharmacy kiosk", "flushing without checking", "giving it away"]'::jsonb,1,'Take-back programs reduce misuse.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.D',3,'Addiction is...','["a talent", "a choice anyone can end quickly", "a disease in which a person cannot stop using a substance despite harm", "a normal habit"]'::jsonb,2,'Addiction changes the brain.','original'),
('115.26.b.15.D',3,'Vaping products can cause...','["healthier lungs", "stronger teeth", "better sports performance", "nicotine addiction and lung damage"]'::jsonb,3,'Vapes contain addictive nicotine.','original'),
('115.26.b.16.A',3,'Short-term effects of misusing prescription drugs may include...','["dizziness, confusion or overdose", "more energy always", "stronger muscles", "better grades"]'::jsonb,0,'Misuse can be immediately dangerous.','original'),
('115.26.b.16.A',3,'A long-term effect of drug misuse is...','["better sleep", "addiction and organ damage", "fewer risks", "improved memory"]'::jsonb,1,'Repeated misuse harms the body.','original'),
('115.26.b.16.B',3,'Using or possessing illegal drugs can lead to...','["extra privileges", "scholarships", "legal consequences such as fines or juvenile detention", "no consequences"]'::jsonb,2,'Drug laws have penalties.','original'),
('115.26.b.16.B',3,'Underage use of alcohol or tobacco is...','["encouraged", "harmless", "required", "against the law"]'::jsonb,3,'Age laws protect youth.','original'),
('115.26.b.17.A',3,'If you suspect a friend is abusing drugs, you should...','["tell a parent, teacher or counselor", "keep it secret", "ignore it", "try the drug"]'::jsonb,0,'Adults can connect them with help.','original'),
('115.26.b.17.A',3,'A way to report suspected drug abuse at school is to...','["do nothing", "talk with a counselor or use an anonymous tip line", "post it online", "confront alone"]'::jsonb,1,'Reporting channels exist.','original'),
('115.26.b.17.B',3,'A sign of possible substance abuse is...','["getting a haircut", "learning a language", "sudden changes in behavior, friends or grades", "joining the band"]'::jsonb,2,'Behavior changes can signal problems.','original'),
('115.26.b.17.B',3,'A physical sign of alcohol use can be...','["faster reflexes", "perfect balance", "bright eyes", "slurred speech and poor coordination"]'::jsonb,3,'Alcohol affects the body.','original'),
('115.26.b.17.C',3,'Who can a student ask for help with substance use?','["a school counselor, parent or doctor", "a stranger", "a dealer", "a rumor"]'::jsonb,0,'Trusted professionals help.','original'),
('115.26.b.17.C',3,'A national helpline for substance use can be reached by...','["calling a random number", "calling the SAMHSA helpline", "guessing", "sending a post"]'::jsonb,1,'Helplines provide free help.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.A',3,'Peer influence on substance use can...','["have no effect", "always protect them", "make someone feel pressured to try it", "make it safe"]'::jsonb,2,'Pressure can push risky choices.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.A',3,'A student who says no to a drug offer is...','["showing weakness", "being rude", "ignoring friends", "using refusal skills"]'::jsonb,3,'Refusing protects health.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
