from (values
('115.26.b.18.B',3,'A positive relationship is one that...','["supports your healthy choices", "pressures you", "demands secrets", "makes fun of you"]'::jsonb,0,'Positive relationships help.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.B',3,'A negative relationship might include someone who...','["helps with homework", "pressures you to drink or smoke", "respects your decisions", "encourages exercise"]'::jsonb,1,'Pressure to use substances is negative.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.C',3,'A social influence on tobacco use is...','["reading a book", "eating vegetables", "seeing friends or family use it", "playing outside"]'::jsonb,2,'Social influences shape choices.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.C',3,'Advertising can influence drinking or vaping by...','["listing health risks only", "providing treatment", "banning stores", "making it look cool or harmless"]'::jsonb,3,'Media can glamorize substances.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.D',3,'The relationship between alcohol and risky behavior is that alcohol...','["lowers judgment and increases risky choices", "boosts coordination", "improves judgment", "prevents accidents"]'::jsonb,0,'Alcohol impairs decision-making.','original'),
('115.26.b.18.D',3,'Using drugs can increase the chance of...','["safer driving", "injury, violence and unsafe sexual behavior", "improved health", "better grades"]'::jsonb,1,'Substances raise risks.','original'),
('115.26.b.19.A',3,'An alternative activity to prevent substance use could be...','["hanging in risky places", "skipping school", "joining a sports team or club", "staying alone online"]'::jsonb,2,'Positive activities reduce risk.','original'),
('115.26.b.19.A',3,'A refusal skill is...','["arguing", "saying maybe", "agreeing", "saying no firmly and leaving"]'::jsonb,3,'Firm refusal works.','original'),
('115.26.b.19.B',3,'If a friend offers you a vape, you could say...','["No thanks, I don''t do that, let''s go somewhere else", "Sure, just once", "Don''t tell anyone", "Maybe later"]'::jsonb,0,'A clear refusal with a suggestion is effective.','original'),
('115.26.b.19.B',3,'When refusing, body language should be...','["looking at the ground", "confident, with eye contact", "silent", "nervous and giggling"]'::jsonb,1,'Confident posture supports your words.','original'),
('115.26.b.19.C',3,'A strategy for avoiding substances is to...','["keep secrets", "hang with users", "stay away from parties where they are used", "go to every party"]'::jsonb,2,'Avoiding settings lowers risk.','original'),
('115.26.b.19.C',3,'Having a code word with a parent that means ''come get me'' helps by...','["increasing pressure", "causing embarrassment", "starting arguments", "giving a safe way to leave a risky situation"]'::jsonb,3,'Planning ahead keeps you safe.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.A',3,'Friendship differs from infatuation because friendship is...','["a long-lasting bond built on trust", "one-sided", "a brief intense crush", "based only on looks"]'::jsonb,0,'Friendship grows over time.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.A',3,'Infatuation is best described as...','["a lifelong bond", "an intense but short-term attraction", "a family tie", "a business deal"]'::jsonb,1,'Infatuation often fades.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.B',3,'Friendships provide a foundation for healthy dating relationships through...','["secrecy", "control", "trust, respect and communication", "jealousy"]'::jsonb,2,'Good relationships build on friendship.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.B',3,'A healthy relationship usually begins with...','["pressure", "ignoring boundaries", "rushing", "being good friends first"]'::jsonb,3,'Friendship lays the groundwork.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.C',3,'A healthy way to express friendship is...','["listening, kindness and spending time together", "controlling the friend", "gossiping", "ignoring them"]'::jsonb,0,'Kind actions show care.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.C',3,'A respectful way to show affection is to...','["demand it", "get consent and honor the other person''s boundaries", "ignore their feelings", "pressure them"]'::jsonb,1,'Respect boundaries.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.D',3,'A characteristic of a healthy dating relationship is...','["name calling", "threats", "mutual respect and honest communication", "jealous control"]'::jsonb,2,'Healthy relationships are respectful.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.D',3,'A warning sign of an unhealthy relationship is...','["respecting space", "sharing interests", "supporting goals", "one person controlling who the other can talk to"]'::jsonb,3,'Control is a red flag.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.E',3,'Each person in a dating relationship should be treated with...','["respect and dignity", "disrespect", "control", "jealousy"]'::jsonb,0,'Everyone deserves respect.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.E',3,'In a healthy relationship, both people...','["follow one person''s orders", "have a voice in decisions", "keep secrets", "avoid talking"]'::jsonb,1,'Equality matters.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.F',3,'Healthy marriages can contribute to families and communities by...','["increasing conflict", "reducing love", "providing stable, supportive environments", "causing neglect"]'::jsonb,2,'Stable families support children.','original'),
('115.26.b.20.F',3,'A strong family relationship helps children by...','["limiting growth", "causing stress", "ignoring needs", "giving them security and guidance"]'::jsonb,3,'Family support builds well-being.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.A',3,'Physical, emotional and sexual abuse are...','["never the victim''s fault and are against the law", "acceptable", "a private matter", "the victim''s fault"]'::jsonb,0,'Abuse is wrong and illegal.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.A',3,'A child who is abused should...','["blame themselves", "tell a trusted adult until someone helps", "keep quiet", "wait for it to stop"]'::jsonb,1,'Telling is the first step.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.B',3,'Sexual harassment can cause the victim to feel...','["happy", "proud", "embarrassed, afraid or unsafe", "popular"]'::jsonb,2,'Harassment hurts emotionally.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.B',3,'A social impact of harassment can be...','["better attendance", "more friends", "greater trust", "avoiding school or activities"]'::jsonb,3,'Victims may withdraw.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.C',3,'A characteristic of an unhealthy relationship is...','["constant put-downs or threats", "kindness", "honesty", "trust"]'::jsonb,0,'Abuse and control are unhealthy.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.C',3,'A harmful relationship may include someone who...','["supports you", "pressures, isolates or hurts you", "listens", "respects you"]'::jsonb,1,'These behaviors are unhealthy.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.D',3,'A way to report suspected abuse is to...','["confront alone", "tell no one", "tell a trusted adult or call a hotline", "wait"]'::jsonb,2,'Reporting gets help started.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.D',3,'A national hotline for child abuse reports can be reached at...','["1-800-NOT-REAL", "a random number", "9-1-1 only for pizza", "1-800-4-A-CHILD"]'::jsonb,3,'The Childhelp hotline provides support.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.E',3,'A healthy sense of self helps people...','["make and respect decisions about their own bodies", "ignore consent", "hide feelings", "give in to pressure"]'::jsonb,0,'Self-respect supports healthy boundaries.','original'),
('115.26.b.21.E',3,'Respecting another person''s decision about their body means...','["pressuring them", "accepting ''no'' every time", "changing their mind", "joking about it"]'::jsonb,1,'Consent matters.','original')
